-- title:
--   Geometric points of a p-divisible group commute with base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $p,h$ be natural numbers and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group over $R$ of height data $(p,h)$ in the sense of the project's structure: a family of levels $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, each a finite free cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebra with $\operatorname{rank}_R = p^{vh}$, together with surjective $R$-bialgebra maps $G.\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernels are the ideals $\mathrm{torsionIdeal}$ generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Let $S$ be a nontrivial commutative $R$-algebra and let $L$ be a commutative ring which is both an $R$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower). Write $G.\mathrm{Point}\,L\,v$ for the set of $R$-algebra maps $G.\mathrm{level}\,v \to L$ with the convolution group law, $G.\mathrm{Points}\,L$ for the direct limit over $v$ of the additive versions of these groups along the level inclusions, and $G.\mathrm{baseChange}\,S$ for the $p$-divisible group over $S$ with levels $S \otimes_R G.\mathrm{level}\,v$. The assertion is that there exist multiplicative isomorphisms $e_v : G.\mathrm{Point}\,L\,v \simeq (G.\mathrm{baseChange}\,S).\mathrm{Point}\,L\,v$ for all $v$ and an additive isomorphism $E : G.\mathrm{Points}\,L \simeq (G.\mathrm{baseChange}\,S).\mathrm{Points}\,L$ such that: the $S$-algebra map underlying $e_v(x)$ sends $s \otimes_R a$ to $s \cdot x(a)$; $E$ carries the level-$v$ canonical map of $x$ to the level-$v$ canonical map of $e_v(x)$; for every $S$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $L$, $e_v$ intertwines the functoriality map induced by $\sigma$ viewed as an $R$-algebra map with the one induced by $\sigma$ as an $S$-algebra map; and $E(\sigma|_R \cdot z) = \sigma \cdot E(z)$ for the corresponding actions on the direct limits.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the $L$-valued points of a $p$-divisible group with base change of the base ring, $G_S(L) = G(L)$ for an $S$-algebra $L$, in a form that records level-by-level identifications and equivariance for the $S$-automorphisms of $L$. It is used to transfer level-preservation and Galois equivariance hypotheses between a $p$-divisible group and its base change, notably in the uniqueness statement for families of bialgebra maps attached to a Galois-equivariant homomorphism of points over a discrete valuation ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_mulEquiv_point_baseChange_and_addEquiv_points_baseChange.lean

